Changes made by FlashRT (2026-11-15)
  - Renamed l3-reference-testing to vla-operator-gate. Rewrote the description
    and added Chinese trigger words.
  - Replaced the ApxInf L3 semantic API, crates/apxinf-cuda-new, Rust tests and
    test-new.sh with FlashRT call sites:
      * torch ops and fvk bindings;
      * StageCapture fixtures (flash_rt/vla/autotune/tools/capture.py,
        artifacts.py);
      * KernelArtifact candidates from ForgeKernel/KernelAgent, and
        patch/port kernels.
  - Changed the fixture rule. ApxInf checks fixtures into the repository;
    FlashRT keeps tensor fixtures in the ignored devlocal/ directory, records
    their sha256, and regenerates seeded draws in tests. This follows FlashRT's
    .gitignore (*.npz, *.bin).
  - Kept the oracle contract: exact typed inputs, decoded quantized values with
    the same scales, an independent public-meaning implementation, and every
    numerics-relevant operand. Kept the coverage rules: run every compatible
    candidate, fail on a silent skip, reject NaN/Inf. Kept the immutable
    thresholds 0.08 / 0.05 / 0.9999 as the default operator gate.
  - Added:
      * the eager same-dtype native baseline and gate validity / INCONCLUSIVE;
      * a second input draw;
      * CUDA Graph capture and replay parity;
      * the sentinel check for in-place and windowed writes;
      * the KernelAgent adapter tolerances
        (tools/external/kernelagent.py: rel-L2 2e-3, cosine 0.99999, relaxed
        against the native error);
      * the distinction from the model-level controller --quality-gate;
      * independence from the generator's own test;
      * where tests live (devlocal while iterating, then a flat tests/ file in
        the candidate worktree's patch);
      * recording the verdict through flash_rt.vla.autotune.decisions with an
        explicit actor.
  - Added references/gate-checklist.md (metric definitions, oracle recipes per
    op_kind, graph parity procedure, test skeleton, report template) and
    agents/openai.yaml.
